In article <10323@elric> bruce@Software.Mitel.COM (The Ghost in The Machine) writes:
>>that four bags of holding full of dilithium crystals and a ton of gold
>>make for a high score.
>Make that "don't make for a high score".  Just kill everything in sight that
>doesn't leave you alone and you will end up with a nice high score.

Actually, make that "do make for a high score."  I just finished the game
with 7,600 diamonds, plus five or six hundred other assorted gems.  My
score due to killing creatures (and I had gone all the way up to level 16
purely by killing creatures - lots of XP's) was only about 1.8 million.
The score I got for the gems was over 30 million.  Makes a bit of a 
difference.

It's kind of cool to have the top score again, but it was funny to have
the third place score the way I did before I finished this game:

1: 3.8 million  Gryfalia, ascended to demigodhood
2: 3.6 million  Stalker, ascended to demigodhood
3: 2.8 million  Endiel (me), killed on level 5 (of 5)

Needless to say, I used the black pudding trick and killed many thousands
of them to get that high a score by level 5.

